@* The trigger is `absolute inset-0`: an invisible sheet over the whole card, not a wrapper
   around it. Nest the media and the text inside and they position absolutely too and escape the
   card. Its own content should be a name and nothing else, because a control with no text is
   announced as its own URL.

   "Open a link or dialog", as shadcn puts it, and both are here. The link opens the file in a
   tab — target="_blank", as shadcn's own accessibility note writes it — so the thread you were
   reading stays where it was. The dialog is for a preview: a preview is not a page, and it has
   nowhere to navigate to.

   The trigger sits BEHIND the actions in the stacking order, so an AttachmentAction and the
   trigger never trap each other. Both stay separately focusable and clickable. *@
<div class="flex w-[340px] flex-col gap-3">
    <Attachment>
        <AttachmentMedia><Icon Name="file" /></AttachmentMedia>
        <AttachmentContent>
            <AttachmentTitle>acme-msa.pdf</AttachmentTitle>
            <AttachmentDescription>Opens in a tab</AttachmentDescription>
        </AttachmentContent>
        <AttachmentActions>
            <AttachmentAction AriaLabel="Remove acme-msa.pdf"><Icon Name="x" /></AttachmentAction>
        </AttachmentActions>
        <AttachmentTrigger Href="/files/acme-msa.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
                           aria-label="Open acme-msa.pdf">
        </AttachmentTrigger>
    </Attachment>

    <Attachment>
        <AttachmentMedia><Icon Name="file-text" /></AttachmentMedia>
        <AttachmentContent>
            <AttachmentTitle>research-summary.pdf</AttachmentTitle>
            <AttachmentDescription>Open preview dialog</AttachmentDescription>
        </AttachmentContent>
        <AttachmentActions>
            <AttachmentAction AriaLabel="Copy link to research-summary.pdf"><Icon Name="copy" /></AttachmentAction>
            <AttachmentAction AriaLabel="Remove research-summary.pdf"><Icon Name="x" /></AttachmentAction>
        </AttachmentActions>
        <AttachmentTrigger Dialog="attachment-preview"
                           aria-label="Preview research-summary.pdf">
        </AttachmentTrigger>
    </Attachment>
</div>

<Dialog Id="attachment-preview" Class="sm:max-w-md">
    <DialogHeader>
        <DialogTitle>research-summary.pdf</DialogTitle>
        <DialogDescription>PDF · 2.4 MB · uploaded 4 March 2026</DialogDescription>
    </DialogHeader>
    <div class="flex h-40 items-center justify-center rounded-md border border-dashed text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        The preview would render here.
    </div>
    <DialogFooter>
        <DialogClose>Close</DialogClose>
        <Button Href="/files/research-summary.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open the file</Button>
    </DialogFooter>
</Dialog>
